# Performance & Optimization

## Database Performance

### Indexing
- Index foreign keys and frequently queried columns
- Use composite indexes for multi-column queries
- For pgvector similarity search, use IVFFlat or HNSW indexes

```sql
-- Foreign key index
CREATE INDEX idx_tickets_created_by ON tickets(created_by);

-- Composite index for common query
CREATE INDEX idx_tickets_status_priority ON tickets(status, priority);

-- pgvector index for embeddings
CREATE INDEX idx_kb_articles_embedding ON kb_articles 
  USING ivfflat (embedding vector_cosine_ops)
  WITH (lists = 100);
```

### Query Optimization
- Use `select()` to fetch only needed columns
- Apply filters server-side, not client-side
- Use pagination for large datasets
- Avoid N+1 queries; use joins or batch fetching

```ts
// Good: Select specific columns, paginate
const { data, error } = await supabase
  .from('tickets')
  .select('id, title, status, created_at, created_by(full_name)')
  .eq('status', 'open')
  .order('created_at', { ascending: false })
  .range(0, 49) // First 50 rows

// Bad: Select all, fetch all rows
const { data } = await supabase.from('tickets').select('*')
```

### Caching Strategies
- Use `revalidate` in `fetch` or route segments for ISR
- Cache frequently accessed data (e.g., KB articles, user profiles)
- Use Supabase Realtime for live updates instead of polling
- Implement stale-while-revalidate pattern

```tsx
// Next.js route-level caching
export const revalidate = 3600 // Revalidate every hour

// Fetch with explicit cache control
const data = await fetch(url, {
  next: { revalidate: 60 } // Revalidate every minute
})

// Supabase query with cache (using React Query or SWR)
const { data: tickets } = useSWR('/api/tickets', fetcher, {
  revalidateOnFocus: false,
  dedupingInterval: 60000 // 1 minute
})
```

## React Performance

### Memoization
- Use `useMemo` for expensive computations
- Use `useCallback` to stabilize function references
- Use `React.memo` to prevent unnecessary re-renders

```tsx
import { useMemo, useCallback, memo } from 'react'

function TicketList({ tickets, onSelect }: TicketListProps) {
  // Memoize filtered list
  const filteredTickets = useMemo(() => {
    return tickets.filter(t => t.status === 'open')
  }, [tickets])
  
  // Stable callback reference
  const handleSelect = useCallback((id: string) => {
    onSelect(id)
  }, [onSelect])
  
  return (
    <div>
      {filteredTickets.map(ticket => (
        <TicketCard key={ticket.id} ticket={ticket} onSelect={handleSelect} />
      ))}
    </div>
  )
}

// Memoize component
export default memo(TicketList)
```

### Code Splitting
- Use dynamic imports for heavy components
- Lazy load non-critical features
- Split routes automatically with App Router

```tsx
import dynamic from 'next/dynamic'

// Lazy load heavy chart component
const AnalyticsChart = dynamic(
  () => import('@/components/analytics/Chart'),
  {
    loading: () => <ChartSkeleton />,
    ssr: false // Disable SSR if not needed
  }
)

// Lazy load modal (only when opened)
const CreateTicketModal = dynamic(
  () => import('@/components/tickets/CreateTicketModal')
)
```

### Virtualization
- Use virtualization for long lists (react-window, react-virtualized)
- Render only visible items
- Improves performance for 100+ items

```tsx
import { FixedSizeList } from 'react-window'

function TicketList({ tickets }: { tickets: Ticket[] }) {
  const Row = ({ index, style }: { index: number, style: React.CSSProperties }) => (
    <div style={style}>
      <TicketCard ticket={tickets[index]} />
    </div>
  )
  
  return (
    <FixedSizeList
      height={600}
      itemCount={tickets.length}
      itemSize={100}
      width="100%"
    >
      {Row}
    </FixedSizeList>
  )
}
```

## Image Optimization

- Use `next/image` for automatic optimization
- Specify width and height to prevent layout shift
- Use appropriate formats (WebP, AVIF)
- Lazy load images below the fold

```tsx
import Image from 'next/image'

<Image
  src="/logo.png"
  alt="Ticket Team Logo"
  width={200}
  height={50}
  priority // For above-the-fold images
/>

<Image
  src={userAvatar}
  alt="User avatar"
  width={40}
  height={40}
  loading="lazy" // Default for below-the-fold
/>
```

## AI Performance

### Streaming Responses
- Stream LLM responses for better UX
- Use Server-Sent Events (SSE) or ReadableStream
- Show partial results as they arrive

```ts
import { GoogleGenerativeAI } from '@google/generative-ai'

export async function streamChatResponse(prompt: string) {
  const genAI = new GoogleGenerativeAI(process.env.GEMINI_API_KEY!)
  const model = genAI.getGenerativeModel({ model: 'gemini-2.0-flash-exp' })
  
  const result = await model.generateContentStream(prompt)
  
  // Stream chunks to client
  const encoder = new TextEncoder()
  const stream = new ReadableStream({
    async start(controller) {
      for await (const chunk of result.stream) {
        const text = chunk.text()
        controller.enqueue(encoder.encode(text))
      }
      controller.close()
    }
  })
  
  return new Response(stream, {
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'text/plain; charset=utf-8' }
  })
}
```

### Embedding Caching
- Cache embeddings for KB articles
- Regenerate only when content changes
- Use database triggers to invalidate cache

```sql
-- Trigger to regenerate embedding on content update
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION regenerate_embedding()
RETURNS TRIGGER AS $$
BEGIN
  -- Set flag to regenerate embedding
  NEW.embedding_stale = TRUE;
  RETURN NEW;
END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql;

CREATE TRIGGER on_kb_article_update
  BEFORE UPDATE OF content ON kb_articles
  FOR EACH ROW
  EXECUTE FUNCTION regenerate_embedding();
```

### Debouncing & Throttling
- Debounce search queries and AI suggestions
- Throttle API calls to prevent rate limiting
- Use abort controllers to cancel stale requests

```tsx
import { useState, useEffect } from 'react'
import { useDebounce } from '@/hooks/useDebounce'

function SearchBar() {
  const [query, setQuery] = useState('')
  const debouncedQuery = useDebounce(query, 500) // 500ms delay
  
  useEffect(() => {
    if (debouncedQuery) {
      // Make API call
      searchKnowledgeBase(debouncedQuery)
    }
  }, [debouncedQuery])
  
  return <input value={query} onChange={e => setQuery(e.target.value)} />
}
```

## Bundle Size

- Analyze bundle with `@next/bundle-analyzer`
- Tree-shake unused code
- Use barrel imports carefully (can prevent tree-shaking)
- Prefer named imports over namespace imports

```ts
// Good: Named imports (tree-shakeable)
import { Button, Dialog } from '@/components/ui'

// Bad: Namespace import (imports entire module)
import * as UI from '@/components/ui'

// Good: Direct imports for large libraries
import debounce from 'lodash/debounce'

// Bad: Imports entire lodash
import { debounce } from 'lodash'
```

## Network Performance

### Parallel Requests
- Fetch independent data in parallel
- Use `Promise.all()` or `Promise.allSettled()`

```ts
// Good: Parallel fetching
const [tickets, users, categories] = await Promise.all([
  fetchTickets(),
  fetchUsers(),
  fetchCategories()
])

// Bad: Sequential fetching (slower)
const tickets = await fetchTickets()
const users = await fetchUsers()
const categories = await fetchCategories()
```

### Request Deduplication
- Next.js automatically deduplicates `fetch` requests in Server Components
- Use React Query or SWR for client-side deduplication

### Compression
- Enable gzip/brotli compression (automatic on Vercel)
- Compress API responses for large JSON payloads

## Monitoring

- Use Next.js Analytics and Speed Insights
- Monitor Core Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS)
- Set performance budgets
- Use Lighthouse CI in build pipeline

```tsx
// Enable Next.js Speed Insights
import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/next'

export default function RootLayout({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) {
  return (
    <html>
      <body>
        {children}
        <SpeedInsights />
      </body>
    </html>
  )
}
```

